  "gaps": [
    "The 22 elective credits are derived, not printed: the program table lists 48 'Remaining General Education and Elective Courses'. 41 general-education credits are required. Business core courses cover 15 of them: CIFS 300 3, ECON 201/203 6, STAT 200 3 and WRTG 112 3. That leaves 26 general-education credits: Communications 9, Arts and Humanities 6, Biological and Physical Sciences 7, and Research and Computing Literacy 4. 48 - 26 = 22 elective credits.",
    "The capture does not name any specific course that must be completed at UMGC. It states residency rules only in general terms: at least 30 credits (normally the final 30), half the major credits, and at least 15 upper-level credits must be completed at UMGC.",
    "General education blocks are discipline-based choices; the capture does not prescribe specific courses for Arts and Humanities, Biological and Physical Sciences, or the general communication/speech course. It only gives recommended courses in the sequencing table."
  ],
